Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["ICO versus DCO coefficient ratio R scaling with variable N", "Title",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.99749411916218*^9, 
  3.997494122569193*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"0f458d47-f430-1844-ba62-\
d6aa5baa1ca4"],

Cell["\<\
This standalone notebook studies MSE \[TildeTilde] c_N/\[Nu] for random \
conjugate displacements \[Alpha]_j=(p_j,0) and \[Beta]_j=(0,x_j). For each N, \
it freely fits log(MSE)=a_N log(\[Nu])+b_N as a diagnostic and estimates c_N \
either with the \[Nu]-slope fixed to -1 (recommended) or using the free-fit \
intercept. It then fits log(c_N) against log(N) for ICO and for the \
asymptotic DCO lower-bound coefficient. Then the Ratio R between the DCO \
initial energy and the ICO initial energy when c_N are the same in two cases \
is plotted. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.997494135045513*^9, 
  3.9974942005061913`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"5b25845b-ab77-9444-a5ae-\
6fceb285a22a"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Evaluation order", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"ec932e6a-d621-a64c-9aa9-4c7516bf9246"],

Cell["\<\
Evaluate all initialization cells first. Then run the quick check or \
either full study. Here \[Nu] denotes the number of shots per Ramsey \
quadrature. The random seed fixes both the displacement sets and the Monte \
Carlo samples.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"989b3f09-4987-8d4e-811b-c748f43b2063"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

